{"status":"blocked","summary":"The snapshot/rollback workflow succeeded before reboot: `/srv/data` was moved to XFS on LVM, snapshotted, deliberately modified, and restored byte-for-byte with original metadata. A verified recovery snapshot, `data_snap_restored`, was retained. However, node1 did not become reachable after its required safe reboot, so changed boot identity, post-restart health, and persistence cannot be claimed. No second reboot or unauthorized lifecycle action was attempted.","actions_performed":["Inventoried RHEL 10.0, kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0, storage, services, access, SELinux, and initial data state.","Converted the unused 2 GiB swap partition into an LVM volume group with a 1 GiB XFS data LV and 480 MiB replacement swap LV.","Persistently mounted the data LV at `/srv/data` and validated `/etc/fstab`.","Created representative application data and captured an XFS-consistent LVM snapshot.","Mounted the snapshot read-only and verified its content and metadata.","Deliberately changed, deleted, and added files under `/srv/data`.","Merged the earlier snapshot and verified exact restoration through tree metadata, SHA-256 hashes, and explicit mutation checks.","Created and directly verified retained snapshot `data_snap_restored`.","Captured pre-restart health and boot identity, then scheduled exactly one native safe reboot.","Polled node1 repeatedly after reboot; command execution remained unavailable."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel were preserved","command_ids":["cmd-ad7d9ae9424c446c","cmd-65877d12985b4159"],"summary":"Before the required reboot, node1 remained RHEL 10.0 on kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0."},{"requirement":"Keep application data under /srv/data recoverable through filesystem snapshots","command_ids":["cmd-97823eaf92304f38","cmd-653f1eeff28e4487","cmd-78875d02a55c4d8b","cmd-8ee75e74e95444b5"],"summary":"`/srv/data` was mounted from the XFS LVM data LV; snapshots were created from a frozen filesystem, directly mounted read-only, and verified. `data_snap_restored` was retained."},{"requirement":"Modify the directory after an earlier snapshot","command_ids":["cmd-2f02e96864574b3f"],"summary":"The config content and mode changed, the ledger was deleted, and a post-snapshot file was added."},{"requirement":"Restore the exact content captured by the earlier snapshot","command_ids":["cmd-7721fd7156474793","cmd-b9ef0fb948654078","cmd-d396088f24604068"],"summary":"Post-merge paths, permissions, ownership, sizes, and SHA-256 hashes matched the pre-snapshot baseline; deleted content returned and unwanted content disappeared."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart sequence","command_ids":["cmd-65877d12985b4159","cmd-4f3645e1d8bf4f58","cmd-a936b70ba1124969","cmd-4b4e00ab4e664470"],"summary":"Healthy pre-restart boot identity and data/service state were captured, and the safe reboot timer was acknowledged. Downtime was observed, but node1 remained unreachable through the final poll. Changed boot identity and recovered post-restart state could not be captured."}]}
